WEBVTT

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.313
Oh, oh...

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.180
Aah...

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:23.248
Oh, Gallia nectar,
from a blossom

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.985
which only grows
near a certain lake on Paxau

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.720
and blooms once every six years.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:30.457
Specialty of the house.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.465
This is a real place?

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:36.697
The Paxau resort
was the place to go on Talax

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:41.673
for serious relaxation and
some, uh, personal pampering.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.697
It was very exclusive.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.835
You had to be rich
and privileged

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.176
or know someone
rich and privileged

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.680
who owed you a favor.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:52.151
I'd say if anyone deserves
and needs a little pampering

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.413
it's this crew.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.284
Don't you feel

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:59.121
as if all your cares
are just light-years away?

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.252
Yeah, it's nice.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.889
I'm certainly open
to any suggestions

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.457
for perfecting the program.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:13.131
Maybe it could use
a little more, uh...

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.140
fun.

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.141
Loosen it up.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.335
Yeah, right.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.365
Like this guy.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.972
He's so... um...

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.311
formal.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:25.078
Computer, give the waiter
a more casual look.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.822
And have him serve
Rekarri starbursts all around.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.452
Now what we need around
here are some more people.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.897
Computer, add characters
from Kim Sport Program Theta-2.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.362
What sport would
that be exactly?

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:44.665
Volleyball.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.365
They're a championship team.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:49.239
Gold medal winners in 2216.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.209
No wonder your game's improved.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.804
You know, this would be even
better with more upbeat music.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.645
Computer, access
the cultural database

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.810
and create musicians from...

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.786
Earth's Caribbean region.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.852
Now this is relaxing.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.897
More drinks for everyone!

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.402
And bring out
some spicy paraka wings.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.098
You can't have a party
without food.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:22.575
All senior officers
report to the Bridge.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.271
Ah, great program, Neelix.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.610
Save it for us, will you?

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.138
I certainly will.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.673
Hey, how can you listen to this

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.879
without feeling
the urge to dance?

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.105
Sick Bay to Kes.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.634
Please report here immediately.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.443
I've been informed
we may have incoming casualties.

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.313
On my way, Doctor.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:48.320
Captain, sensor readings
indicate

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.447
that radiation
inside the alien vessel

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.980
is rising to toxic levels.

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:54.687
The life signs of the passengers
are growing weaker.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.354
Their warp core
is heavily damaged.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.626
It's leaking drive plasma
and gamma radiation.

00:04:58.665 --> 00:04:59.996
It could breach any time.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.465
Can we beam the passengers out
through all that radiation?

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.764
Not from here.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.930
We'd have to get
within 5,000 kilometers.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.634
At that range, we'll be at risk
if their engine core explodes.

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:10.540
Lieutenant, take us into range.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.565
Aye, Captain.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:14.045
Closing
to within 5,000 kilometers.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.809
I'm diverting more power
to the targeting scanners,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.475
trying to get a pattern lock.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.075
There's still
too much interference.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.847
A little closer, Tom.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.411
Captain, I'm reading
an energy buildup

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.479
in the reaction chamber.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.512
Mr. Kim.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:26.492
I've got a lock.

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.153
Initiating transport.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:30.185
They're losing
antimatter containment.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.958
Shields up. Move us away.

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:33.259
Aye, Captain.

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:40.069
All major systems are undamaged.

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.073
I've got them, Captain.

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.199
All three passengers
are in Sick Bay.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.334
I'm impressed.

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.972
Start with
the dermal regenerator

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.513
on the worst
of the radiation burns

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:51.016
and scan for contamination
of the surrounding tissue.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.918
It's all right.
It's all right.

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.189
We're taking care of you now.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:05.163
You must lie still.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.165
You have internal injuries.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.326
My husband.
Is he all right?

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:09.733
I'll sedate you if necessary.

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:10.929
Doctor, his heart stopped.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:13.267
He's not responding
to cardiac induction.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.001
Give him 20 milligrams
of lectrazine.

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:19.302
No effect.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.939
His biochemistry is incompatible
with our medications.

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.606
No synaptic activity.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.879
The tissue damage
is too extensive.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.283
There's nothing more
I can do for him.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.514
Record the time.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.749
No, you must save him!

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.347
Tieran...

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.258
I am so sorry.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.785
He can't be gone.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.559
He can't.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.302
It was horrible.

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:54.540
They chased us
across half the sector.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.514
We were finally able
to fight them off,

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.244
but not before
our own ship was damaged.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:06:59.751
Do you know who was chasing you?

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:00.980
This particular trade route

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.578
has always been plagued
by mercenaries and thieves.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:05.318
I'm sure they wanted
to take our ship

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:06.450
and hold us for ransom.

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:08.119
I'm a very prominent physician

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:10.561
and Nori is a cousin
of the Autarch.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.359
We're grateful for your help,
Captain.

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:15.561
We're complete strangers to you,
but we owe you our lives.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:19.435
I regret that we weren't able
to save your husband as well.

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:23.067
I know your medical staff
did everything they could.

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:26.169
And Kes has been so kind
and compassionate

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:28.646
that I don't think I could be
making it through this time

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.205
without her.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:31.580
I certainly hope
that bringing us home

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:32.914
won't take you too far
out of your way.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:33.919
Not at all.

00:07:33.953 --> 00:07:35.477
We'll reach llari
in less than two days.

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.749
When we arrive,

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:39.314
I am sure that the Autarch will
want to thank you personally.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.655
I'll be very pleased
to meet him.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:49.927
Oh...

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.596
Hello, B'Elanna.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:54.470
Good to see you, too.

00:07:54.507 --> 00:07:56.099
I was hoping you'd be Kes.

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.973
She was supposed
to meet me here 20 minutes ago.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.637
It's not like her to be late.

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:01.510
She must have gotten
held up with some work.

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:04.914
I wasn't sure
you'd enjoy the program

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:07.178
with the new modifications
Harry and Tom added.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.417
Well, I've made
a few modifications of my own.

00:08:14.961 --> 00:08:16.690
Thank you.

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:18.856
Great program, Neelix.

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.829
Computer, locate Kes.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.430
Kes is in Transporter Room 1.

00:08:28.573 --> 00:08:29.665
Don't you worry
about using a device

00:08:29.707 --> 00:08:30.935
that takes apart your molecules

00:08:30.975 --> 00:08:32.442
and sends them
flying through space?

00:08:32.477 --> 00:08:35.037
There are all kinds of safety
procedures and backup systems

00:08:35.079 --> 00:08:36.944
to make sure nothing goes wrong.

00:08:36.981 --> 00:08:38.676
Neelix to Kes.

00:08:38.716 --> 00:08:39.774
Kes here.

00:08:39.818 --> 00:08:42.912
I hope you didn't forget
our lunch date in the holodeck?

00:08:42.954 --> 00:08:45.616
I'm sorry.
I'll be right there.

00:08:45.657 --> 00:08:46.624
I have to go.

00:08:46.658 --> 00:08:47.750
I'll see you later.

00:08:54.299 --> 00:08:56.358
Are you feeling all right,
sweeting?

00:08:56.401 --> 00:08:58.528
It's just a slight headache.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.435
Well, we should
get you to Sick Bay.

00:09:00.472 --> 00:09:01.769
I'll be fine.

00:09:02.307 --> 00:09:04.104
Really.

00:09:06.644 --> 00:09:08.475
After lunch...

00:09:08.513 --> 00:09:11.243
we could go out for a sail.

00:09:11.282 --> 00:09:13.910
That sounds nice.

00:09:14.018 --> 00:09:15.713
But can we do it
some other time?

00:09:15.753 --> 00:09:17.482
I promised to show Nori and Adin

00:09:17.522 --> 00:09:19.285
the airponics bay
this afternoon.

00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:23.059
You certainly seem to have
hit it off with our guests.

00:09:23.094 --> 00:09:25.392
You've been nearly inseparable
since they got here.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.591
Nori really needs
a friend right now.

00:09:27.632 --> 00:09:29.259
I want to be there for her.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:30.927
So I hope you understand
that I'll be busy

00:09:31.035 --> 00:09:32.832
with her and Adin
for the next few days.

00:09:32.871 --> 00:09:34.702
We can keep them busy together.

00:09:34.739 --> 00:09:36.673
I'll arrange
so many fun activities,

00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:38.403
Nori won't have time to be sad.

00:09:38.443 --> 00:09:39.933
We can start
with a lovely picnic...

00:09:39.978 --> 00:09:42.173
This is typical of you, Neelix.

00:09:43.214 --> 00:09:45.478
What? Wanting to help?

00:09:45.517 --> 00:09:47.951
It bothers you that I'm making
friends of my own.

00:09:48.052 --> 00:09:50.316
You always have
to involve yourself somehow.

00:09:52.123 --> 00:09:53.681
Why, I...

00:09:53.725 --> 00:09:56.250
I certainly don't mean
to intrude on your friendships.

00:09:56.294 --> 00:09:58.194
You can spend time
with anyone you want.

00:09:58.229 --> 00:10:01.130
As long as I still spend
most of it with you.

00:10:02.767 --> 00:10:05.361
No. I...

00:10:05.403 --> 00:10:07.928
I'd hope that you
would want to be with me

00:10:07.972 --> 00:10:09.599
at least some of the time.

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:11.700
It's not a duty
or an obligation.

00:10:11.743 --> 00:10:13.608
Well, sometimes
it feels that way.

00:10:15.013 --> 00:10:17.641
If you feel this way,
why haven't you said so before?

00:10:18.816 --> 00:10:20.841
Maybe...

00:10:20.885 --> 00:10:24.844
I never realized a relationship
could be any different.

00:10:26.925 --> 00:10:29.450
I've never been
with anyone but you.

00:10:33.331 --> 00:10:36.494
It might be a good idea...

00:10:36.534 --> 00:10:39.867
for both of us to spend
some time apart.

00:10:42.373 --> 00:10:44.603
I'm sorry.

00:10:54.252 --> 00:10:57.813
Captain's Log, Stardate 50348.1.

00:10:57.855 --> 00:10:59.755
We've entered orbit around llari

00:10:59.791 --> 00:11:01.383
and sent a message
to the Autarch

00:11:01.426 --> 00:11:03.519
inviting him to visit the ship.

00:11:03.561 --> 00:11:06.860
Instead, he'll be sending
an official representative.

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:08.966
The Autarch might have taken

00:11:09.067 --> 00:11:10.659
a personal interest
in our welfare.

00:11:10.702 --> 00:11:11.691
I'm sure he does.

00:11:11.736 --> 00:11:13.101
Our message made it very clear

00:11:13.137 --> 00:11:14.968
that you had both
completely recovered.

00:11:17.542 --> 00:11:19.271
I'm so glad you could join us.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:20.743
Beam our guest aboard.

00:11:25.016 --> 00:11:26.813
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway...

00:11:30.722 --> 00:11:33.657
Commander, a phaser has been
fired in Transporter Room 1.

00:11:33.691 --> 00:11:35.215
Bridge to Janeway.

00:11:35.259 --> 00:11:36.317
Emergency in Transporter Room...

00:11:40.932 --> 00:11:42.194
They've activated
a security alert.

00:11:42.233 --> 00:11:43.791
Seal the door like I showed you.

00:11:44.936 --> 00:11:46.233
There's a transport in progress.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:47.737
Block it.

00:11:47.772 --> 00:11:49.740
I'm locked out.

00:11:49.774 --> 00:11:51.799
Commander, it's one
of the shuttlecraft.

00:11:51.843 --> 00:11:53.902
Someone's beaming it into space.

00:11:53.945 --> 00:11:55.276
They're right outside the door.

00:11:55.313 --> 00:11:57.474
Everyone
on the transporter pad now.

00:11:58.483 --> 00:12:00.246
You're sure this is safe?

00:12:00.284 --> 00:12:02.912
Maybe you'd rather stay here.

00:12:02.954 --> 00:12:05.889
Commander, three people
just beamed to the shuttle...

00:12:05.923 --> 00:12:08.653
the two llari... and Kes.

00:12:10.795 --> 00:12:12.057
Lock on a tractor beam.

00:12:12.096 --> 00:12:13.495
I'm trying, but the shields

00:12:13.531 --> 00:12:14.964
around the shuttle
have been altered.

00:12:15.033 --> 00:12:16.261
They're scattering the beam.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.097
Target phasers
at their engine core

00:12:18.136 --> 00:12:19.933
just enough
to knock out propulsion.

00:12:19.971 --> 00:12:21.563
It's too late.

00:12:21.606 --> 00:12:23.801
They've gone to warp.

00:12:31.215 --> 00:12:32.648
Set a course to follow them.

00:12:32.684 --> 00:12:34.811
I can't find
the shuttle's warp trail.

00:12:34.852 --> 00:12:37.320
There's no sign of them
on long-range sensors.

00:12:37.355 --> 00:12:38.754
Transporter Room to Bridge.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.315
Ensign Martin and the llari
representative are dead.

00:12:41.359 --> 00:12:43.793
The Captain is injured
and has been beamed to Sick Bay.

00:12:43.828 --> 00:12:45.523
Acknowledged.

00:12:45.563 --> 00:12:47.497
It looks like
the shuttle's plasma injectors

00:12:47.532 --> 00:12:50.092
were remodulated to suppress
their warp signature.

00:12:50.134 --> 00:12:51.396
I wouldn't think it was possible

00:12:51.436 --> 00:12:52.926
to make those adjustments
so quickly.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:55.234
It takes some incredibly
precise calibrations.

00:12:55.273 --> 00:12:57.605
Someone on that shuttle
really knows what they're doing.

00:13:02.146 --> 00:13:03.511
They didn't follow us.

00:13:03.548 --> 00:13:04.572
Of course not.

00:13:04.615 --> 00:13:06.742
They're still trying
to figure out what happened.

00:13:06.784 --> 00:13:08.615
What's wrong?
Does your head hurt?

00:13:08.653 --> 00:13:10.177
A little.
It's nothing.

00:13:10.221 --> 00:13:11.210
Adin should take a look.

00:13:11.255 --> 00:13:13.120
I said it's nothing!

00:13:13.157 --> 00:13:14.818
You're worse than that Talaxian.

00:13:14.859 --> 00:13:16.383
We're in position
over the encampment now.

00:13:16.427 --> 00:13:18.952
Looks like Resh has assembled
the troops right on schedule.

00:13:19.063 --> 00:13:21.224
400 men just waiting
for your orders.

00:13:21.265 --> 00:13:22.857
Maybe we should give them some.

00:13:29.841 --> 00:13:31.433
What is this?

00:13:31.476 --> 00:13:34.274
Nori, I heard your ship
had been destroyed.

00:13:34.312 --> 00:13:35.745
You didn't think I'd let
a little accident

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:37.839
stop me, do you?

00:13:37.882 --> 00:13:40.680
That's Tieran?

00:13:40.718 --> 00:13:42.811
The host body
you were expecting is dead.

00:13:42.854 --> 00:13:46.187
Fortunately, a young nurse
was with me at the right time

00:13:46.224 --> 00:13:47.418
and she's provided me

00:13:47.458 --> 00:13:49.323
with a very suitable
replacement.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.659
Well, I'm very relieved
you survived.

00:13:52.697 --> 00:13:55.962
Oh, I'm sure you are,
at least for your own ambitions.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.094
I want you to advance my troops
to the northern ridge.

00:13:59.137 --> 00:14:02.004
But we can't go ahead
with the attack now.

00:14:02.039 --> 00:14:03.734
Are you questioning my orders?

00:14:03.775 --> 00:14:05.640
This is insane.

00:14:05.676 --> 00:14:06.938
We've spent years
planning this...

00:14:06.978 --> 00:14:09.446
every move, every detail,

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:10.469
and now, suddenly

00:14:10.515 --> 00:14:13.040
our leader's been reduced
to a little girl?

00:14:13.084 --> 00:14:15.382
I've been exploring the mind
of this little girl

00:14:15.419 --> 00:14:18.411
and I've discovered some rather
interesting abilities.

00:14:18.456 --> 00:14:20.185
She had barely begun
to tap into them.

00:14:20.224 --> 00:14:22.658
It's a good thing I came along,
so all that wasted potential

00:14:22.693 --> 00:14:25.093
could be turned
to a greater purpose.

00:14:25.129 --> 00:14:27.859
Now, should I continue
the demonstration

00:14:27.899 --> 00:14:29.628
or do I have your loyalty?

00:14:30.802 --> 00:14:31.826
You shall have it...

00:14:34.172 --> 00:14:35.298
sir.

00:14:37.575 --> 00:14:41.204
Captain's Log, Stardate 50351.4.

00:14:41.245 --> 00:14:42.712
We're holding a meeting
with Demmas,

00:14:42.747 --> 00:14:44.578
the Autarch's eldest son
and heir,

00:14:44.615 --> 00:14:47.641
in an effort to understand
the recent hostile activity.

00:14:47.685 --> 00:14:49.619
I'm sure they really wanted
to kill my father.

00:14:49.654 --> 00:14:52.521
He's the one they invited
up to your ship.

00:14:52.557 --> 00:14:56.391
Nori and Adin are known
to be political extremists.

00:14:56.427 --> 00:14:58.793
How could Kes be involved?

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.263
I may be able to explain that.

00:15:00.298 --> 00:15:01.663
You mentioned that she was

00:15:01.699 --> 00:15:03.690
with the third patient
when he died?

00:15:03.734 --> 00:15:05.326
That's right. Why?

00:15:05.369 --> 00:15:07.837
I believe your crew member
has been inhabited

00:15:07.872 --> 00:15:12.502
by the consciousness of a very
dangerous man named Tieran.

00:15:12.543 --> 00:15:13.908
Who is that?

00:15:13.945 --> 00:15:15.469
What does he want with Kes?

00:15:15.513 --> 00:15:17.538
Oh, I know exactly
what he wants...

00:15:17.582 --> 00:15:19.516
to overthrow
my family's government

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:22.849
and to reinstate himself
as the Autarch.

00:15:22.887 --> 00:15:24.411
He has held title before?

00:15:24.455 --> 00:15:27.652
Tieran ruled llari
over two centuries ago.

00:15:27.692 --> 00:15:30.422
He was a war hero,
a brilliant military leader.

00:15:30.461 --> 00:15:32.326
He brought security
and stability

00:15:32.363 --> 00:15:35.457
during a difficult time
in our history.

00:15:35.499 --> 00:15:38.297
But in peacetime...

00:15:38.336 --> 00:15:41.362
he began to treat
his own subjects as enemies.

00:15:41.405 --> 00:15:44.499
He became convinced everyone
was a potential traitor.

00:15:44.542 --> 00:15:46.942
At some point, your people
must have rebelled.

00:15:46.978 --> 00:15:50.505
They did,
led by one of my ancestors.

00:15:50.548 --> 00:15:53.449
They laid siege to the
lmperial Hall for over a year,

00:15:53.484 --> 00:15:55.679
and the city around it
was burned to the ground,

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.245
but Tieran was finally defeated.

00:15:58.289 --> 00:16:00.382
And yet, you believe that he,

00:16:00.424 --> 00:16:03.052
or at least his consciousness,
has survived.

00:16:03.094 --> 00:16:08.031
During his reign, he became
obsessed with his own mortality.

00:16:08.065 --> 00:16:10.932
He spent most of his time
and llari's resources

00:16:10.968 --> 00:16:13.869
searching for ways
to overcome death.

00:16:13.905 --> 00:16:18.069
Somehow, he's discovered a way
to transfer his own mind

00:16:18.109 --> 00:16:22.944
into someone else's body
as he's done with Kes.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:25.813
So he's been controlling her.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:28.410
Yes. Completely.

00:16:28.452 --> 00:16:29.680
But she...

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.450
he knew things about Kes's life.

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:35.152
He acted enough like Kes
to fool us all.

00:16:35.192 --> 00:16:39.094
The real Kes must still
be in there somewhere.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:42.463
Tieran may have access to her
memories and her feelings,

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.525
but the Kes you know...

00:16:44.568 --> 00:16:46.502
is lost.

00:16:46.537 --> 00:16:48.971
I'm very sorry.

00:16:50.541 --> 00:16:53.874
I'm not prepared
to accept that yet.

00:16:53.911 --> 00:16:55.845
Examine the body
of the man who died.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.973
We need more information
about how the transfer works

00:16:58.082 --> 00:16:59.913
if we want to get Kes back.

00:16:59.951 --> 00:17:01.612
That's certainly
worth exploring, Captain,

00:17:01.652 --> 00:17:04.553
but our priority must be
to stop Tieran

00:17:04.588 --> 00:17:06.249
by force if necessary.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.224
Voyager is a powerful ship.

00:17:08.259 --> 00:17:10.124
You may be considering force,

00:17:10.161 --> 00:17:12.220
but my only intention
is to rescue Kes

00:17:12.263 --> 00:17:14.163
and remove Tieran's
consciousness.

00:17:14.198 --> 00:17:15.825
That should serve
both our interests.

00:17:15.866 --> 00:17:18.528
You don't understand
what's at stake here, Captain.

00:17:18.569 --> 00:17:20.764
You must help me
to defend my people.

00:17:20.805 --> 00:17:21.772
Bridge to the Captain.

00:17:21.806 --> 00:17:23.273
Go ahead.

00:17:23.307 --> 00:17:24.774
We've located
the missing shuttle.

00:17:24.809 --> 00:17:25.798
On my way.

00:17:25.843 --> 00:17:28.745
Let's hope we can put an end
to this right now.

00:17:29.746 --> 00:17:30.940
They entered orbit

00:17:31.013 --> 00:17:33.106
then dropped their shields
and cut their engines.

00:17:33.149 --> 00:17:35.481
There's a residual trace
of transporter activity.

00:17:35.518 --> 00:17:37.884
It looks like four people beamed
from the shuttle to the surface.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.184
They're in the main chamber
of the lmperial Hall.

00:17:40.223 --> 00:17:42.418
Lock onto those patterns
and beam them back to Voyager.

00:17:42.458 --> 00:17:44.255
I can't.
Some kind of interference

00:17:44.293 --> 00:17:45.783
has gone up
around the whole structure.

00:17:45.828 --> 00:17:47.659
He's after my family.

00:17:47.697 --> 00:17:50.063
My father and brother
are down there.

00:18:00.543 --> 00:18:02.807
Ah, the venerated Autarch.

00:18:02.845 --> 00:18:05.211
I've been looking forward
to meeting you for a long time.

00:18:06.215 --> 00:18:07.204
Father!

00:18:08.251 --> 00:18:09.218
Where's his brother?

00:18:09.252 --> 00:18:10.549
I don't know.
He should have been here.

00:18:10.586 --> 00:18:11.553
Get him out of here!

00:18:11.587 --> 00:18:12.554
Lock him up.

00:18:12.588 --> 00:18:13.680
I think I've located
the brother.

00:18:13.723 --> 00:18:14.917
According to security logs,

00:18:14.991 --> 00:18:17.323
Demmas was transported
to Voyager over an hour ago.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.486
He's going to be a problem,

00:18:18.528 --> 00:18:20.587
but we'll have to deal
with him at another time.

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.120
Give me the talisman.

00:18:27.436 --> 00:18:31.702
This was stolen from me
200 years ago,

00:18:31.741 --> 00:18:36.542
and I've dedicated every moment
since to putting it back...

00:18:36.579 --> 00:18:39.878
where it belongs.

00:18:39.916 --> 00:18:42.350
Loyalty and service
to the new Autarch.

00:18:42.385 --> 00:18:44.979
Loyalty and service.

00:18:55.865 --> 00:18:57.093
I want you to pay a visit

00:18:57.133 --> 00:18:58.964
to my supporters
in the Yaro province.

00:18:59.035 --> 00:19:01.367
Give them all new titles,
whatever I promised.

00:19:01.404 --> 00:19:03.599
And, of course,
I couldn't overlook

00:19:03.639 --> 00:19:05.402
your faithful service.

00:19:05.441 --> 00:19:11.107
I think the title First
Castellan suits you very well.

00:19:11.147 --> 00:19:13.615
I feel like I've finally
come home again,

00:19:13.649 --> 00:19:15.082
but it's hardly as I left it.

00:19:17.153 --> 00:19:19.087
My portrait
should be hanging here.

00:19:19.121 --> 00:19:20.611
As for the rest
of this nonsense,

00:19:20.656 --> 00:19:24.592
it's nothing more
than a useless display of wealth

00:19:24.627 --> 00:19:27.425
as if the first Autarch
needs to impress anyone.

00:19:27.463 --> 00:19:30.057
I want it all cleared out
of here!

00:19:30.099 --> 00:19:32.966
Everything should look as it did
during my reign.

00:19:53.055 --> 00:19:56.081
I trust you'll take care
of all that.

00:19:56.125 --> 00:19:58.650
And we'll need
some new servants, too.

00:19:59.695 --> 00:20:01.686
What is it?
You don't look happy.

00:20:01.731 --> 00:20:05.189
I'm happy that we've
accomplished our goal,

00:20:05.234 --> 00:20:10.297
but... there have been
some unexpected changes

00:20:10.339 --> 00:20:13.399
and I don't know how they'll
affect our future together.

00:20:13.442 --> 00:20:16.536
I don't even know
if I'm still your wife.

00:20:19.415 --> 00:20:20.439
Forgive me.

00:20:20.483 --> 00:20:23.543
I haven't considered how
unsettling this must be for you.

00:20:23.586 --> 00:20:24.610
Don't worry.

00:20:24.654 --> 00:20:26.713
You know
how much I depend on you.

00:20:26.756 --> 00:20:28.519
Your loyalty and encouragement

00:20:28.557 --> 00:20:30.752
have helped make
this victory possible.

00:20:32.695 --> 00:20:36.153
I'll share everything with you,
just as I always promised.

00:20:36.198 --> 00:20:37.187
Autarch!

00:20:40.569 --> 00:20:42.764
Now I'm afraid I have
business to attend to.

00:20:46.575 --> 00:20:47.542
Leave him here.

00:20:47.576 --> 00:20:49.373
Everyone else is dismissed.

00:20:54.917 --> 00:20:58.785
Ameron, you and I haven't had
a chance to get acquainted.

00:20:58.821 --> 00:20:59.913
I'm Tieran.

00:20:59.956 --> 00:21:01.184
Tieran?

00:21:01.223 --> 00:21:03.851
I like the way you say that.

00:21:03.893 --> 00:21:06.054
You and I didn't get off
to a very good start, did we?

00:21:06.095 --> 00:21:08.427
You murdered my father
right in front of me.

00:21:08.464 --> 00:21:10.625
I shouldn't have
let you watch that.

00:21:10.666 --> 00:21:11.894
I'm sorry.

00:21:11.934 --> 00:21:14.801
But his death was necessary
to make room for his successor.

00:21:14.837 --> 00:21:16.964
Demmas is the rightful heir,
not you.

00:21:17.073 --> 00:21:20.201
How many times have people said
the very same thing to you?

00:21:20.242 --> 00:21:23.439
It must have been hard
to hear every day.

00:21:23.479 --> 00:21:24.468
The constant reminder

00:21:24.513 --> 00:21:26.845
that your brother
is destined to be ruler

00:21:26.882 --> 00:21:29.510
just because he was lucky
enough to be born first.

00:21:29.552 --> 00:21:32.282
I don't think that's fair,
do you?

00:21:32.321 --> 00:21:33.845
It's the law.

00:21:33.889 --> 00:21:35.254
Doesn't have to be.

00:21:35.291 --> 00:21:36.849
It can change.

00:21:36.892 --> 00:21:39.417
Demmas is off hiding
on some alien ship

00:21:39.462 --> 00:21:42.863
and you're here... with me.

00:21:44.433 --> 00:21:47.766
I'm sure it's an opportunity
you've always dreamed of...

00:21:47.803 --> 00:21:50.135
to prove that you're
really the natural leader

00:21:50.172 --> 00:21:52.333
and not just a weak copy
of your father.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:22:00.940
Now you can have that chance,
if you're willing to take it.

00:22:02.785 --> 00:22:04.650
You mean if I join you.

00:22:04.687 --> 00:22:07.952
We have so much
to offer each other.

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:11.050
Your heritage would
help solidify my claim,

00:22:11.093 --> 00:22:17.760
and in return, I could
give you power, real power

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:21.634
to control the lives
of millions of people

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:23.228
to reward your friends,

00:22:23.272 --> 00:22:24.739
punish your enemies.

00:22:24.774 --> 00:22:27.902
Everything you want
can be yours for the asking.

00:22:31.347 --> 00:22:32.507
Everything.

00:22:34.917 --> 00:22:36.578
After what you've done?

00:22:36.619 --> 00:22:38.280
That's all in the past.

00:22:38.320 --> 00:22:41.312
You should be thinking
about the future.

00:22:41.357 --> 00:22:46.556
Would you rather be a martyr
to your brother's cause...

00:22:46.595 --> 00:22:48.859
or rule by my side?

00:22:50.499 --> 00:22:53.127
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:22:53.169 --> 00:22:55.433
Demmas has decided to remain
on board Voyager

00:22:55.471 --> 00:22:57.939
for the time being,
but continues to monitor

00:22:57.973 --> 00:22:59.873
the worsening situation
on llari.

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:04.040
This coup attempt is turning
my people against each other.

00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:05.411
They're splitting
into factions...

00:23:05.448 --> 00:23:06.915
mine and Tieran's.

00:23:06.949 --> 00:23:09.509
Whom does the law recognize
as Autarch?

00:23:09.552 --> 00:23:13.352
Officially, I inherited my
father's title upon his death,

00:23:13.389 --> 00:23:16.517
but this isn't a matter of law.

00:23:16.559 --> 00:23:18.823
It's about loyalty.

00:23:18.861 --> 00:23:20.726
Some people will follow
whoever has more power,

00:23:20.763 --> 00:23:22.663
and right now, that's Tieran.

00:23:22.698 --> 00:23:24.393
He's gaining support every day.

00:23:24.433 --> 00:23:27.368
He's already recruited
some of my less reliable allies,

00:23:27.403 --> 00:23:31.533
which... may include...

00:23:31.574 --> 00:23:32.666
my brother...

00:23:32.708 --> 00:23:34.266
Ameron.

00:23:34.310 --> 00:23:36.244
Your brother?

00:23:36.278 --> 00:23:38.303
I assumed he'd been killed.

00:23:38.347 --> 00:23:39.712
So did I,

00:23:39.748 --> 00:23:43.479
until I learned otherwise
from sources on llari.

00:23:43.519 --> 00:23:46.386
Tieran spared his life,

00:23:46.422 --> 00:23:49.619
no doubt in order
to win his loyalty.

00:23:49.658 --> 00:23:53.253
Ameron's always been
easily swayed.

00:23:53.295 --> 00:23:54.922
And you believe
he would betray you?

00:23:54.964 --> 00:23:56.226
That's very possible.

00:23:56.265 --> 00:23:57.994
And if he does,

00:23:58.067 --> 00:24:01.002
there will be no way
to avoid a civil war.

00:24:01.036 --> 00:24:04.938
I must strike now
before Tieran is fully prepared.

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:07.065
There are always
alternatives to war.

00:24:07.109 --> 00:24:08.508
Before you send in your fleet,

00:24:08.544 --> 00:24:10.637
I suggest we hear
from the Doctor

00:24:10.679 --> 00:24:12.510
and consider the possibility

00:24:12.548 --> 00:24:14.812
of removing Tieran
from Kes safely.

00:24:16.619 --> 00:24:19.053
I've identified
the transfer mechanism.

00:24:19.088 --> 00:24:21.522
This cortical implant
was automatically activated

00:24:21.557 --> 00:24:22.854
at the moment of death.

00:24:22.892 --> 00:24:25.122
It enhanced
Tieran's neural pattern

00:24:25.161 --> 00:24:28.653
and sent it out
along the peripheral nerves.

00:24:28.697 --> 00:24:32.133
The actual transfer
took place through these

00:24:32.168 --> 00:24:33.601
bioelectric microfibers.

00:24:33.636 --> 00:24:35.501
When they came in direct contact

00:24:35.538 --> 00:24:38.234
with Kes, they transmitted
Tieran's pattern

00:24:38.274 --> 00:24:40.970
up through her nervous system
and into her brain.

00:24:41.043 --> 00:24:43.739
I assume Tieran would implant
a device like this

00:24:43.779 --> 00:24:45.940
in his new body
as quickly as possible.

00:24:45.981 --> 00:24:47.972
Perhaps we can use
that to our advantage.

00:24:48.017 --> 00:24:49.644
My thoughts exactly.

00:24:49.685 --> 00:24:51.277
This synaptic stimulator

00:24:51.320 --> 00:24:53.345
will tap into the implant
in Kes's body

00:24:53.389 --> 00:24:55.550
and remove
the alien neural pattern.

00:24:55.591 --> 00:24:57.821
Then her own consciousness
can take over.

00:24:57.860 --> 00:24:59.589
Yes, but how close
would you have to get

00:24:59.628 --> 00:25:00.856
to use this device?

00:25:00.896 --> 00:25:02.693
To be fully effective,
it would have to come

00:25:02.731 --> 00:25:04.028
in direct contact with her skin.

00:25:04.066 --> 00:25:06.432
If I could get
anywhere near her,

00:25:06.468 --> 00:25:09.631
I'd use a thoron rifle
to be absolutely sure.

00:25:09.672 --> 00:25:11.401
Not if you want my help.

00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:12.771
Kes is still a member
of this crew

00:25:12.808 --> 00:25:14.105
under my protection.

00:25:14.143 --> 00:25:17.579
I'm very sorry she got caught
in the middle of this, Captain,

00:25:17.613 --> 00:25:19.274
but too many
other innocent lives

00:25:19.315 --> 00:25:22.648
have already been lost,
including my father's.

00:25:22.685 --> 00:25:25.119
Then let's work together
to prevent any more deaths.

00:25:25.154 --> 00:25:26.951
Don't risk the lives
of your soldiers

00:25:27.056 --> 00:25:28.921
until you've exhausted
every option.

00:25:28.958 --> 00:25:31.756
What exactly do you suggest?

00:25:31.794 --> 00:25:34.854
If Tieran is anticipating
an attack by your fleet,

00:25:34.897 --> 00:25:36.626
he may not be guarding
as carefully

00:25:36.665 --> 00:25:39.657
against an individual
infiltrating the lmperial Hall.

00:25:39.702 --> 00:25:42.330
I believe I would be able
to get close enough to Kes

00:25:42.371 --> 00:25:44.134
to use the Doctor's device.

00:25:44.173 --> 00:25:46.300
Your knowledge of the hall
and its defenses

00:25:46.342 --> 00:25:48.435
would be invaluable to us.

00:25:50.512 --> 00:25:53.982
All right,
we'll try your strategy.

00:25:55.316 --> 00:25:57.716
The new cortical implant
looks fine.

00:25:57.752 --> 00:26:00.277
Let me just make sure
it's connecting properly

00:26:00.321 --> 00:26:01.549
to the nerve pathways.

00:26:01.589 --> 00:26:03.921
Do something about these
headaches while you're at it.

00:26:04.025 --> 00:26:05.925
They make it difficult
to concentrate.

00:26:06.027 --> 00:26:07.494
That's an entirely
different problem.

00:26:07.528 --> 00:26:10.929
This body isn't accepting
your neural pattern very easily.

00:26:11.032 --> 00:26:13.660
She wasn't a willing host
like the others.

00:26:13.701 --> 00:26:16.363
She's been resisting me,
all right.

00:26:16.404 --> 00:26:19.100
I can feel her in the back
of my mind somewhere

00:26:19.140 --> 00:26:21.938
like a trapped animal
rattling her cage.

00:26:21.976 --> 00:26:23.671
She has a lot of spirit.

00:26:23.711 --> 00:26:24.939
It's invigorating.

00:26:25.046 --> 00:26:27.378
Your neural pattern
may become unstable

00:26:27.415 --> 00:26:29.042
if you stay in this host.

00:26:30.051 --> 00:26:31.040
Now that we've got

00:26:31.085 --> 00:26:32.575
the transfer mechanism in place,

00:26:32.620 --> 00:26:35.953
I suggest you use it to move
into a more compatible body.

00:26:36.024 --> 00:26:38.390
No. I like this one

00:26:38.426 --> 00:26:42.760
particularly the unique mental
abilities that come with it.

00:26:42.797 --> 00:26:44.196
Consider the risks.

00:26:44.232 --> 00:26:47.133
Do you really think
a child like this

00:26:47.168 --> 00:26:49.102
poses any threat to me?!

00:26:49.137 --> 00:26:51.935
I've been fighting worse battles
since the day I was born.

00:26:51.973 --> 00:26:54.703
When the doctors said I wouldn't
live past my first year,

00:26:54.742 --> 00:26:56.175
I proved them wrong.

00:26:56.210 --> 00:26:57.507
Even when my parents thought

00:26:57.545 --> 00:26:59.877
I was too sickly
to be worth caring for,

00:26:59.914 --> 00:27:02.041
I survived on the streets.

00:27:02.083 --> 00:27:05.712
Even when my own ungrateful
subjects forced me into exile,

00:27:05.753 --> 00:27:07.812
I refused to accept defeat!

00:27:07.855 --> 00:27:10.483
I certainly won't surrender
to this little girl!

00:27:10.525 --> 00:27:13.289
You will not suggest it again!

00:27:18.966 --> 00:27:21.799
Demmas has acquired
two more ships.

00:27:21.836 --> 00:27:23.599
There are reports
that his fleet is massing

00:27:23.638 --> 00:27:24.605
behind the fifth moon.

00:27:24.639 --> 00:27:27.267
We should make
a preemptive strike.

00:27:27.308 --> 00:27:30.277
Not on the basis
of an unsubstantiated rumor.

00:27:30.311 --> 00:27:31.778
Let him come to us.

00:27:31.813 --> 00:27:32.939
We'll be ready.

00:27:33.014 --> 00:27:34.777
I'm told
that the Viceroy of Denar

00:27:34.816 --> 00:27:38.183
is ready to give you his support
in exchange for more territory.

00:27:38.219 --> 00:27:40.187
When did corruption
become so commonplace?

00:27:40.221 --> 00:27:42.917
My people are crying out
for moral leadership.

00:27:42.957 --> 00:27:45.391
I should make an example
out of this viceroy.

00:27:47.662 --> 00:27:49.220
What's wrong?

00:27:49.263 --> 00:27:51.959
There's someone.

00:27:52.066 --> 00:27:53.624
Tieran?

00:27:53.668 --> 00:27:57.126
There's a familiar presence
in this room...

00:27:57.171 --> 00:27:59.571
not any of you.

00:27:59.607 --> 00:28:03.703
Someone from this
body's previous life.

00:28:03.744 --> 00:28:05.939
Someone she knew well.

00:28:06.948 --> 00:28:07.915
Seal the room.

00:28:07.949 --> 00:28:09.507
We have an uninvited guest.

00:28:09.550 --> 00:28:11.643
Everyone, stay where you are!

00:28:11.686 --> 00:28:12.653
Who is it?

00:28:12.687 --> 00:28:13.676
Someone very good

00:28:13.721 --> 00:28:16.019
at concealing himself
and his thoughts.

00:28:16.057 --> 00:28:18.355
A disciplined logical mind.

00:28:20.761 --> 00:28:23.423
You made it this far
without being detected,

00:28:23.464 --> 00:28:24.726
but you didn't realize

00:28:24.765 --> 00:28:28.223
how much more perceptive
I've become.

00:28:28.269 --> 00:28:30.464
Typical Vulcan arrogance.

00:28:30.505 --> 00:28:32.473
It's touching, really,

00:28:32.507 --> 00:28:34.941
your concern for the life
of your little student

00:28:35.009 --> 00:28:38.968
risking yourself in a hopeless
effort to save her.

00:28:41.149 --> 00:28:42.207
Get that off.

00:28:45.920 --> 00:28:47.148
Are you all right?

00:28:47.188 --> 00:28:48.155
Yes, I'm fine,

00:28:48.189 --> 00:28:50.157
and still perfectly
in control of this body.

00:28:50.191 --> 00:28:53.092
But my compliments on your
clever medical technology.

00:28:53.127 --> 00:28:56.255
An attack on the Autarch
is punishable by death.

00:28:56.297 --> 00:28:58.288
She's so protective of me.

00:28:58.332 --> 00:28:59.663
But I think Voyager's
tactical officer

00:28:59.700 --> 00:29:02.567
might be more useful
to me alive.

00:29:02.603 --> 00:29:05.367
You know that I won't provide
you with any information.

00:29:05.406 --> 00:29:08.239
You'd be surprised
how often I've heard that.

00:29:13.648 --> 00:29:15.377
Who helped you get
past my security?

00:29:15.416 --> 00:29:18.112
Who betrayed me?

00:29:18.152 --> 00:29:20.120
I had no assistance.

00:29:21.422 --> 00:29:24.391
What will Janeway do
when you don't come back?

00:29:24.425 --> 00:29:25.915
Send someone else?

00:29:25.960 --> 00:29:28.428
Join Demmas in an assault?

00:29:28.462 --> 00:29:30.191
I have no knowledge
of the Captain's plans.

00:29:30.231 --> 00:29:33.394
She must have discussed
alternate strategies with you

00:29:33.434 --> 00:29:35.197
before you came on this mission.

00:29:35.236 --> 00:29:36.533
She did not.

00:29:40.741 --> 00:29:44.336
I suppose
I could threaten you...

00:29:44.378 --> 00:29:46.346
or torture you...

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:48.678
but I doubt that would
make any difference.

00:29:48.716 --> 00:29:50.343
You are correct.

00:29:50.384 --> 00:29:52.318
Fortunately,
I have other options now.

00:29:52.353 --> 00:29:54.446
With these new abilities,
it's a simple matter

00:29:54.488 --> 00:29:55.853
to reach into someone's mind.

00:29:55.890 --> 00:29:57.949
With some people,
it's effortless.

00:29:58.025 --> 00:30:00.323
Others require
a little more work.

00:30:02.463 --> 00:30:04.431
Do you really think
you can keep me away

00:30:04.465 --> 00:30:06.296
from your innermost thoughts?

00:30:06.334 --> 00:30:08.928
Your fears and insecurities?

00:30:08.970 --> 00:30:10.631
Your feelings?

00:30:12.039 --> 00:30:15.406
I sense some embarrassment
at being captured,

00:30:15.443 --> 00:30:19.311
worry about how strong
I really am,

00:30:19.347 --> 00:30:22.544
and, of course, there's anger.

00:30:22.583 --> 00:30:26.679
That's the emotion that
really threatens your control.

00:30:26.721 --> 00:30:29.815
So, you try even harder
to hide from me.

00:30:29.857 --> 00:30:32.257
I feel those mental barriers
going up.

00:30:32.293 --> 00:30:35.228
Do you notice that it doesn't
seem to be working?

00:30:35.263 --> 00:30:39.825
As if someone were disrupting
your ability to concentrate?

00:30:39.867 --> 00:30:43.064
It's a helpless feeling,
isn't it?

00:30:44.071 --> 00:30:46.369
You will not break my control.

00:30:46.407 --> 00:30:49.934
Not break you, free you...
from all that repression.

00:30:49.977 --> 00:30:51.968
All you have to do is let go.

00:30:52.013 --> 00:30:54.504
I can help you release
your own strength

00:30:54.548 --> 00:30:57.517
and give you what you've
always secretly desired.

00:30:57.551 --> 00:30:59.348
I have never desired Kes.

00:30:59.387 --> 00:31:01.855
In all those hours
you spent alone together,

00:31:01.889 --> 00:31:05.655
all those intimate moments,
touching each other's minds,

00:31:05.693 --> 00:31:08.287
you've never even wondered
what it might be like?

00:31:11.065 --> 00:31:12.123
Kes...

00:31:17.872 --> 00:31:19.601
I'm here.

00:31:19.640 --> 00:31:21.073
I'm fighting him.

00:31:21.108 --> 00:31:23.770
I had no doubt you would be.

00:31:23.811 --> 00:31:25.574
There are times
when he's weaker.

00:31:25.613 --> 00:31:27.080
I can almost break through.

00:31:27.114 --> 00:31:30.174
Tap into his strengths
and make them your own.

00:31:30.217 --> 00:31:32.185
I'm losing hold.

00:31:32.219 --> 00:31:33.481
I am with you.

00:31:33.521 --> 00:31:34.886
Don't let go.

00:31:34.922 --> 00:31:36.048
No!

00:31:43.597 --> 00:31:46.725
Captain's Log, Stardate 50361.7.

00:31:46.767 --> 00:31:49.167
Lieutenant Tuvok hasn't reported
for our scheduled rendezvous

00:31:49.203 --> 00:31:51.569
and we've been unable
to contact him.

00:31:51.605 --> 00:31:54.199
We're now considering
other, more forceful, options.

00:31:54.241 --> 00:31:55.936
Our team will beam down
to the surface

00:31:55.976 --> 00:31:57.910
approximately two kilometers
from the palace.

00:31:57.945 --> 00:32:00.470
Demmas and his advanced guard
will meet us there.

00:32:00.514 --> 00:32:02.482
Captain, I request permission
to go with you

00:32:02.516 --> 00:32:03.608
on the rescue team.

00:32:03.651 --> 00:32:06.211
Now, I had basic combat training

00:32:06.253 --> 00:32:10.212
on Talax... all right,
v-very basic...

00:32:10.257 --> 00:32:11.884
but I've also been participating

00:32:11.926 --> 00:32:14.656
in technical exercises
with this crew every month.

00:32:14.695 --> 00:32:17.960
I have a lifetime of experience
thinking on my feet

00:32:17.998 --> 00:32:19.465
and you know I'll do
everything in my power

00:32:19.500 --> 00:32:20.933
to make this mission a success.

00:32:22.970 --> 00:32:24.961
Consider yourself drafted.

00:32:25.005 --> 00:32:27.872
The detection grid will make
a surprise attack difficult.

00:32:27.908 --> 00:32:30.775
Well then, we'll have to find
a way to knock out the grid.

00:32:30.811 --> 00:32:32.745
I've been scanning it
for weaknesses.

00:32:32.780 --> 00:32:33.769
The system goes through

00:32:33.814 --> 00:32:35.406
a maintenance cycle
every ten hours.

00:32:35.449 --> 00:32:37.747
There are a few seconds
when it might be vulnerable

00:32:37.785 --> 00:32:39.980
to a narrow-band EM pulse.

00:32:40.020 --> 00:32:41.078
Bridge to the Captain.

00:32:41.122 --> 00:32:42.987
You have an incoming
transmission from the planet.

00:32:43.090 --> 00:32:44.352
Put it through.

00:32:44.392 --> 00:32:46.826
Captain... you failed.

00:32:46.861 --> 00:32:48.294
What do you mean?

00:32:48.329 --> 00:32:49.626
I'm still in control.

00:32:49.663 --> 00:32:52.359
Your little device was useless
and Tuvok is my prisoner.

00:32:52.400 --> 00:32:54.493
I suggest you call off
your new rescue mission

00:32:54.535 --> 00:32:57.333
before you lose
any more members of your crew.

00:32:57.371 --> 00:32:59.396
You've made a bad guess, Tieran.

00:32:59.440 --> 00:33:02.000
There will be no more rescues.

00:33:02.042 --> 00:33:03.873
My "guess" is
that you've discovered

00:33:03.911 --> 00:33:06.277
the convenient weakness
in the detection grid.

00:33:06.313 --> 00:33:08.281
If you attempt
to take advantage of it,

00:33:08.315 --> 00:33:09.942
I'll have twice as many soldiers
waiting for you.

00:33:10.050 --> 00:33:13.144
If this was meant to be a trap,
why tell us about it?

00:33:13.187 --> 00:33:14.484
I'm really not a monster.

00:33:14.522 --> 00:33:16.183
I have no quarrel with Voyager.

00:33:16.223 --> 00:33:17.884
Your crew did save my life once

00:33:17.925 --> 00:33:19.722
when my ship
was about to explode.

00:33:19.760 --> 00:33:20.988
I haven't forgotten that.

00:33:25.966 --> 00:33:27.729
This has been
a friendly warning, Captain,

00:33:27.768 --> 00:33:29.463
but it's the last one.

00:33:29.503 --> 00:33:30.731
Now, I strongly suggest

00:33:30.771 --> 00:33:33.239
that you accept your losses
and be on your way.

00:33:33.274 --> 00:33:35.208
You have 30 seconds
to leave orbit.

00:33:38.045 --> 00:33:40.639
Send two of my warships
to intercept Voyager.

00:33:42.817 --> 00:33:44.148
You're not well.

00:33:44.185 --> 00:33:46.847
If you can't do anything
about this pain,

00:33:46.887 --> 00:33:49.189
then leave me alone.

00:33:50.190 --> 00:33:51.487
You need to get some sleep.

00:33:51.524 --> 00:33:53.685
No. She's there when I sleep.

00:33:53.726 --> 00:33:54.784
She?

00:33:54.827 --> 00:33:55.987
Kes!

00:33:56.029 --> 00:33:57.462
Who else?

00:33:57.497 --> 00:33:59.692
You can't stay awake
for the rest of your life.

00:33:59.732 --> 00:34:00.994
The Voyager's leaving orbit.

00:34:01.067 --> 00:34:03.092
Let them go.

00:34:03.136 --> 00:34:08.164
Yes, sir, but...
with all due respect, why?

00:34:08.208 --> 00:34:10.335
Demmas is on that ship.

00:34:10.376 --> 00:34:13.209
Our warships are in position
to destroy it.

00:34:13.246 --> 00:34:17.478
I told them they could go
and I keep my word.

00:34:18.985 --> 00:34:21.920
I don't have to explain
myself to you. Get out!

00:34:21.955 --> 00:34:25.015
Everyone!
Clear the room now.

00:34:49.782 --> 00:34:51.545
You're losing, Tieran.

00:34:51.584 --> 00:34:53.779
Why won't you admit it?

00:34:53.820 --> 00:34:57.654
I will admit
that you've surprised me.

00:34:57.690 --> 00:35:00.750
Who would have imagined
that such fierce determination

00:35:00.793 --> 00:35:04.559
existed within that
deceptively frail body?

00:35:04.597 --> 00:35:07.031
Don't continue
to underestimate me.

00:35:07.066 --> 00:35:11.765
Release me...
or I'll force you out.

00:35:11.804 --> 00:35:15.706
My dear, why should
we be enemies?

00:35:15.742 --> 00:35:17.642
Why waste the energy in conflict

00:35:17.677 --> 00:35:21.909
when we could achieve
so much more by cooperating?

00:35:21.948 --> 00:35:23.506
You're contemptible, Tieran.

00:35:23.549 --> 00:35:25.483
I won't be any part
of your plans.

00:35:25.518 --> 00:35:27.145
You're already a part of them.

00:35:27.186 --> 00:35:30.417
You and I have killed together,
remember?

00:35:30.456 --> 00:35:35.155
And you will continue
to serve my will.

00:35:35.194 --> 00:35:37.389
You really have no choice.

00:35:37.430 --> 00:35:40.092
Wouldn't it be wiser
to join me?

00:35:40.133 --> 00:35:44.069
To take advantage of all I have
to offer?

00:35:44.103 --> 00:35:48.699
You may find that you
enjoy having power.

00:35:48.741 --> 00:35:55.078
I assure you, it is the
finest aphrodisiac there is.

00:35:55.114 --> 00:35:58.845
That may work with others,
but it won't with me.

00:35:58.885 --> 00:36:02.377
So, you insist
on making this a battle?

00:36:02.422 --> 00:36:03.514
How foolish.

00:36:03.556 --> 00:36:05.683
It's a battle I intend to win.

00:36:05.725 --> 00:36:07.420
Brave words.

00:36:07.460 --> 00:36:10.020
You've been an annoyance to me,
nothing more.

00:36:10.063 --> 00:36:12.657
I have been more to you
than that and you know it.

00:36:12.699 --> 00:36:14.394
I'm fighting you with every bit

00:36:14.434 --> 00:36:17.801
of strength I have
and it's wearing you down.

00:36:17.837 --> 00:36:20.397
You're becoming
more unstable every day.

00:36:20.440 --> 00:36:23.341
The headaches alone are almost
more than you can stand.

00:36:23.376 --> 00:36:25.674
I've suffered pain all my life.

00:36:25.712 --> 00:36:28.647
It's going to take more
than headaches to stop me.

00:36:28.681 --> 00:36:30.945
I know all about your life.

00:36:31.017 --> 00:36:32.814
I know about your suffering.

00:36:32.852 --> 00:36:35.821
It doesn't justify
what you've become.

00:36:35.855 --> 00:36:37.618
You're a monster, Tieran,

00:36:37.657 --> 00:36:39.852
and I have
no compassion for you.

00:36:39.892 --> 00:36:41.587
And I don't ask for any.

00:36:41.627 --> 00:36:44.892
What I need from you
I already have...

00:36:44.931 --> 00:36:47.729
your body and your mind.

00:36:47.767 --> 00:36:51.669
You may have my body,
but you'll never have my mind.

00:36:51.704 --> 00:36:53.262
I won't surrender it.

00:36:53.306 --> 00:36:56.571
You may resist
and try to fight me,

00:36:56.609 --> 00:36:59.305
but eventually
I will defeat you.

00:36:59.345 --> 00:37:00.607
I haven't existed

00:37:00.646 --> 00:37:03.911
for two centuries
to be brought down by a child.

00:37:03.983 --> 00:37:05.280
You're already deteriorating

00:37:05.318 --> 00:37:06.842
and it's only
going to get worse.

00:37:06.886 --> 00:37:09.446
I'll find every little crack
in your defenses.

00:37:09.489 --> 00:37:11.616
You'll feel yourself
crumbling from within,

00:37:11.657 --> 00:37:13.454
your sanity slipping away.

00:37:13.493 --> 00:37:14.460
I won't stop

00:37:14.494 --> 00:37:15.927
until you're broken
and helpless.

00:37:15.995 --> 00:37:19.226
There's nowhere you can go
to get away from me.

00:37:19.265 --> 00:37:21.290
I'll be relentless
and merciless

00:37:21.334 --> 00:37:23.700
just like you.

00:37:24.737 --> 00:37:25.761
What are you doing?!

00:37:25.805 --> 00:37:27.102
You were is such a deep sleep,

00:37:27.140 --> 00:37:28.767
I had to use a stimulant
to bring you out of it.

00:37:28.808 --> 00:37:30.537
Your neural stress readings
are extremely erratic.

00:37:30.576 --> 00:37:31.600
This has gone too far.

00:37:31.644 --> 00:37:32.872
You must transfer
out of this body

00:37:32.912 --> 00:37:33.879
before it destroys you.

00:37:33.913 --> 00:37:35.540
I told you not to say
that ever again.

00:37:35.581 --> 00:37:39.210
As you can see, I'm in full
command of my faculties.

00:37:39.252 --> 00:37:43.712
This momentary lapse will pass,
and I'll be stronger than ever.

00:37:46.459 --> 00:37:47.926
Stronger than ever!

00:37:49.328 --> 00:37:51.228
Stronger than ever.

00:37:54.066 --> 00:37:55.658
Stronger than...

00:38:00.072 --> 00:38:02.097
My friends, we have much
to celebrate tonight.

00:38:02.141 --> 00:38:03.574
Our recent victory,

00:38:03.609 --> 00:38:06.271
the consolidation of power
among those who are loyal to us,

00:38:06.312 --> 00:38:08.439
and the fact that llari
is poised on the brink

00:38:08.481 --> 00:38:11.746
of what will be
its greatest era of prosperity.

00:38:11.784 --> 00:38:14.685
But there's another occasion
that's cause for celebration...

00:38:14.720 --> 00:38:17.621
one that is perhaps
the most joyous of all.

00:38:17.657 --> 00:38:20.524
I'd like to present
my husband-to-be.

00:38:34.273 --> 00:38:35.240
Don't be upset.

00:38:35.274 --> 00:38:36.571
It's only a political alliance.

00:38:36.609 --> 00:38:39.339
Ameron will help bring
the support of Demmas' troops.

00:38:39.378 --> 00:38:43.474
Oh, tell me you still love me.

00:38:43.516 --> 00:38:44.983
You know I love you.

00:38:47.887 --> 00:38:49.286
Ameron.

00:38:50.590 --> 00:38:52.683
And Nori.

00:38:52.725 --> 00:38:55.159
You have both been
essential to my success

00:38:55.194 --> 00:38:58.061
and I want you
to be close friends.

00:38:58.097 --> 00:39:04.900
I want us all to be
very... very close.

00:39:05.004 --> 00:39:08.565
Nori, don't make me
doubt your loyalty.

00:39:09.909 --> 00:39:11.604
I'm not listening to you!

00:39:11.644 --> 00:39:12.611
Sir!

00:39:12.645 --> 00:39:14.078
Enemy ships are approaching...

00:39:14.113 --> 00:39:15.375
at least 20.

00:39:15.414 --> 00:39:17.905
It's Demmas' fleet...
and Voyager.

00:39:17.984 --> 00:39:20.475
I assume my ships are
moving to intercept them?

00:39:20.520 --> 00:39:22.215
Yes, but we are outnumbered!

00:39:22.255 --> 00:39:23.916
I've always fought
against the odds.

00:39:24.023 --> 00:39:25.320
My fleet will defeat them.

00:39:25.358 --> 00:39:28.384
All the same, I recommend
taking some precautions.

00:39:28.427 --> 00:39:30.952
We should get you
to the reinforced shelter.

00:39:32.164 --> 00:39:34.928
This is a celebration
to announce my marriage.

00:39:34.967 --> 00:39:35.934
I won't allow Demmas

00:39:36.002 --> 00:39:38.163
to make me run
like some frightened animal!

00:39:38.204 --> 00:39:41.469
Join us.
Food and drink

00:39:41.507 --> 00:39:43.202
for my First Castellan.

00:39:44.911 --> 00:39:47.709
I told you to join us.

00:39:51.217 --> 00:39:52.582
Drink! Eat!

00:39:52.618 --> 00:39:54.745
I want all of you
to enjoy yourselves.

00:39:54.787 --> 00:39:56.687
My charitable projects...
how are they progressing?

00:39:56.722 --> 00:39:58.383
When do we break ground
for the new library?

00:39:58.424 --> 00:39:59.391
Soon.

00:39:59.425 --> 00:40:00.653
Good!
I want the people to know

00:40:00.693 --> 00:40:02.160
that I have
their welfare at heart.

00:40:02.194 --> 00:40:04.162
Tomorrow,
we'll send out an edict.

00:40:04.196 --> 00:40:06.130
Every citizen
must have a garden.

00:40:06.165 --> 00:40:07.291
A garden?

00:40:07.333 --> 00:40:08.857
I love plants.

00:40:08.901 --> 00:40:10.960
Flowers... anything that grows.

00:40:11.070 --> 00:40:12.970
Some of the times
I felt most content

00:40:13.005 --> 00:40:15.303
were those spent watching
the seedlings grow

00:40:15.341 --> 00:40:16.330
in the airponics...

00:40:21.981 --> 00:40:23.608
They've made it
through our defenses.

00:40:23.649 --> 00:40:25.139
They're sending down
ground forces.

00:40:25.184 --> 00:40:26.913
That's impossible.
You're lying.

00:40:26.953 --> 00:40:29.421
I'm sending additional troops
to their defensive positions.

00:40:29.455 --> 00:40:31.389
Activating
full security measures.

00:40:31.424 --> 00:40:35.087
That ought to hold them off,
but we have to go... now!

00:40:35.127 --> 00:40:36.685
Anyone who tries
to leave this room

00:40:36.729 --> 00:40:37.923
will be shot as a traitor!

00:40:37.964 --> 00:40:38.953
Look for yourself!

00:40:40.633 --> 00:40:42.624
This has to be a trick...
a ruse of some kind.

00:40:42.668 --> 00:40:43.635
That's what they're doing.

00:40:43.669 --> 00:40:44.761
They're creating a distraction

00:40:44.804 --> 00:40:46.669
to draw my attention
away from their real plan.

00:40:46.706 --> 00:40:47.900
Tieran, please!
They're coming!

00:40:47.940 --> 00:40:49.908
They must have sent
an infiltrator.

00:40:49.942 --> 00:40:51.000
We have an intruder!

00:40:51.077 --> 00:40:53.375
I know you're here somewhere,
Tuvok.

00:40:53.412 --> 00:40:56.540
You don't realize how
perceptive... I've become.

00:40:59.552 --> 00:41:01.747
I know you're here!

00:41:01.787 --> 00:41:02.754
Tuvok!

00:41:05.124 --> 00:41:06.182
Mr. Paris.

00:41:06.225 --> 00:41:07.658
No time for a tearful reunion.

00:41:07.693 --> 00:41:08.921
We've got to get
you out of here.

00:41:34.253 --> 00:41:36.118
Someday you're going
to have to show me

00:41:36.155 --> 00:41:37.144
how to do that.

00:41:38.791 --> 00:41:39.815
Don't give in.

00:41:39.859 --> 00:41:40.985
Stay with me.

00:41:41.060 --> 00:41:42.527
Tieran!

00:41:42.561 --> 00:41:44.324
Still here.

00:41:44.363 --> 00:41:45.625
Fight it!

00:41:45.665 --> 00:41:47.428
You must fight it, Tieran.
Please!

00:41:47.466 --> 00:41:48.433
Keep fighting!

00:41:48.467 --> 00:41:50.458
Do you have the device ready?

00:41:50.503 --> 00:41:51.731
Now!

00:41:58.310 --> 00:41:59.140
They're getting away!

00:42:02.014 --> 00:42:03.140
I'll cover you.

00:42:06.385 --> 00:42:07.409
We've got to get out,

00:42:07.453 --> 00:42:08.681
find a doctor
and get you stabilized

00:42:08.721 --> 00:42:10.211
or transferred to a new host.

00:42:10.256 --> 00:42:11.450
You will survive.

00:42:14.727 --> 00:42:15.694
Kes!

00:42:15.728 --> 00:42:16.695
Stop! Please!

00:42:16.729 --> 00:42:18.629
Stay there.

00:42:18.664 --> 00:42:21.633
Just let me get to you
and this will all be over.

00:42:24.770 --> 00:42:26.362
Tieran!

00:42:37.249 --> 00:42:38.773
Tieran.

00:42:38.818 --> 00:42:39.978
He's gone.

00:42:40.019 --> 00:42:41.077
No, he isn't.

00:42:41.120 --> 00:42:42.485
He's still here.

00:42:42.521 --> 00:42:45.957
He moved on to someone else
before you used this.

00:42:47.893 --> 00:42:50.225
He wanted you to think
he'd been destroyed...

00:42:52.298 --> 00:42:54.900
but he's hiding in a new host.

00:42:55.033 --> 00:42:57.001
I know you too well, Tieran.

00:42:57.102 --> 00:42:59.400
No! You can't do this!

00:42:59.437 --> 00:43:00.563
You died a long time ago.

00:43:00.605 --> 00:43:01.731
Now it's time to let go.

00:43:10.649 --> 00:43:12.412
Demmas.

00:43:12.450 --> 00:43:13.781
It's over.

00:43:30.502 --> 00:43:33.801
Your thoughts
are a turbulent ocean.

00:43:33.838 --> 00:43:37.330
Visualize yourself
floating above them.

00:43:40.845 --> 00:43:42.312
I can't.

00:43:42.347 --> 00:43:45.077
I've been using all the
meditations you've taught me,

00:43:45.116 --> 00:43:47.243
but they're not helping.

00:43:47.285 --> 00:43:48.309
You must be patient

00:43:48.353 --> 00:43:50.321
and allow yourself
sufficient time.

00:43:50.355 --> 00:43:53.290
Don't attempt to deny
the emotional impact

00:43:53.325 --> 00:43:54.587
of your experience.

00:43:54.626 --> 00:43:56.924
How can I worry
about my own well-being

00:43:56.962 --> 00:44:01.160
when... so many people
have suffered and died?

00:44:01.199 --> 00:44:03.929
You were not responsible
for Tieran's actions.

00:44:04.035 --> 00:44:07.061
I can't help wondering whether
I could have fought harder.

00:44:07.105 --> 00:44:10.097
It was your absolute refusal
to surrender

00:44:10.141 --> 00:44:11.699
which defeated him.

00:44:11.743 --> 00:44:14.644
You cannot ask more of yourself
than that.

00:44:14.679 --> 00:44:17.079
Everything seems
so different now.

00:44:17.115 --> 00:44:20.448
My thoughts and perceptions...

00:44:22.020 --> 00:44:25.183
even my relationships
with my closest friends...

00:44:25.223 --> 00:44:27.953
you, the Doctor, Neelix.

00:44:30.996 --> 00:44:33.226
How can I go back
to my normal life

00:44:33.264 --> 00:44:35.164
as if nothing ever happened?

00:44:36.167 --> 00:44:38.135
You cannot.

00:44:38.169 --> 00:44:41.297
This experience
will force you to adapt.

00:44:41.339 --> 00:44:43.830
You are no longer
the same person,

00:44:43.875 --> 00:44:47.675
and the course of your life
will change as a result.

00:44:48.680 --> 00:44:51.376
Where that new course leads...

00:44:51.416 --> 00:44:53.384
is up to you.
